<title>RUSSIA: Russian first-half GDP falls 0.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian first-half GDP falls 0.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gross domestic product (GDP) in the first half of 1997 was 1.232 trillion roubles, down 0.2 percent from a year ago in inflation-adjusted terms, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>GDP in June was four-percent higher than a year earlier.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN GDP			  Q2 97     Q1 97     Q2 96</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	  -0.6	+0.3	-5</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN GDP			  June 97   May 97    June 96</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	+4	  +0.8	+3</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	  0	   -0.4	-7</p>
<p>Note - Official Russian data tend to underreport a growing private sector in the economy.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($1 = 5,773 roubles)</p>
